  "country": "SI",
  "description": "Months (1-12) transcribed cell by cell from the Ministry of Agriculture's 'Naša super hrana' seasonal charts; each item comes from exactly one chart (see 'source'). Tabela 1-3 legend: dark green 'obdobje z močno ponudbo' (period of strong supply) is given as 'peak'; light green 'obdobje ponudbe' (period of supply) and dark green together are given as 'months', so peak is a subset of months. '(H)' in Tabela 1 means 'zelenjava, ki jo kmetje lahko skladiščijo v hladilnicah' (vegetables farmers can keep in cold storage); it marks no months and is given as 'coldStorable': true. Tabela 3 lists 19 apple varieties in thirds of a month; the single 'apple' item has every month in which any variety has any marked third in 'months', and every month in which any variety has a dark third in 'peak'. The 'Dostopnost slovenskega sadja skozi leto' chart is used only for fruit not in Tabela 1-3; it marks availability with an icon per month, has no legend and no peak or storage marking, so those items have 'months' only. None of the charts marks storage months, so no item has 'storage'. Items not listed are not covered by the sources.",
